      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T22:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about also adding `EC_CMD_MEMORY_DUMP_CLEAR`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5566,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 5566,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d75f5c82_25b6130f",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 5566,
      "author": {
        "id": 1519424
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T05:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There isn\u0027t a command for the host to register memory regions for dumping, so I\u0027m not sure there\u0027s a use case for the host clearing?",
      "parentUuid": "5f9a2822_9a365e73",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5566,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 5566,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49ce57e5_7120739d",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 5566,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T22:58:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking it might make some tests easier.  But if there\u0027s not use case from the host, then I agree it\u0027s not needed.",
      "parentUuid": "d75f5c82_25b6130f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5566,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 5566,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b9559a7_8706a8e5",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 5580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T22:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The host command protocol already provides a versioning mechanism.  I don\u0027t think this is needed to future proof the command.  I also can\u0027t think of an instance where we would have 64-bit support, but only needed a single offset for all memory regions.  It seems more likely we would need to each `struct ec_response_memory_dump_get_entry_info` to include a 64-bit address.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5579,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 5580,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
