      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T22:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It could be useful to add arguments to dump a specific index, or limit the total number of bytes returned.\n\nAn optional `clear` parameter would be helpful too.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 223,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e858ab50_0154d2af",
        "filename": "util/ectool.cc",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 1519424
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T05:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I considered this, but the index is arbitrary (order in which memory is registered). It does serve as a rough paging mechanism.\n\nA another option would be to take an address and size. Obviously not all of the requested memory would be available, but it could print all the memory that is available in the requested range.\n\nI will revisit this option.",
      "parentUuid": "fba4786f_64ee884d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 223,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
