      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T22:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could use `SYS_INIT()` to have the zephyr memory dump module self initialize instead of requiring a public routine.\n\nAlso, should this be done after `vboot_main()` - in which case you would need to use `DECLARE_HOOK(HOOK_INIT,...)` instead of `SYS_INIT`.  The kernel runs `SYS_INIT` calls before starting the application main function.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d1b7c19_2aad25e4",
        "filename": "zephyr/app/ec/ec_app_main.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1519424
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T05:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good suggestion. Switched to `HOOK_INIT`. This simplifies a few things.",
      "parentUuid": "27eeab93_e1c8ab9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
